 Run notes per `VERSION` stamp. **Trio:** VERSION + CHANGELOG.md + ACTIONS.
 
+## 0.5.27 — 2026-11-19 — Data update: proposal to build, Churchill Falls record to 16 Nov
+
+Reframe the campus from a feasibility study to a proposal to build across pages, metadata, `llms.txt`, manifest, OG copy, desk data and the `/ask` knowledge file. Every honest limit stays: not approved, not funded, not under construction, no megawatts reserved, no nation asked, nothing sent to NL Hydro, no site chosen. `/ask` knowledge follows the 27 October proposal version, drops ACOA lines and candidate site names, and keeps the Compute Strategy apart from the ISED 100 MW call. New knowledge-bans test. "Labrador AI campus" wording finished, including the `/about` and `/compute` search titles. Home and `/brief` Ottawa heading now cites Budget 2026 (500 MW of sovereign AI compute access, chapter 5). Churchill Falls record adds the 28 October House motion defeated 16–21 (Hansard p. 2886) and the 13 and 16 November Québec / Premier quotes (reported, CBC and VOCM); the line about the agreements returning to the House is removed. Past `/engage` events dropped; 21 Oct and 17 Nov marked passed. `DESK_VERIFIED` unchanged (2026-10-14) until merge day. OG PNGs regenerated. Preview only; Tom merges.
+
 ## 0.5.25 — 2026-10-29 — Durable /ask question log
 
 `POST /api/ask` writes `ask.received` as soon as the question is parsed, then inserts `ask_questions` with status `received` (service-role, RLS on, no anon). The same row is updated to `answered` or `failed` with provider, model, fallback flag, and error. Writes run through `after()` so they do not delay the first token. Missing env, a missing table, or a write error logs a warning and the assistant still answers. No IP or user-agent; optional coarse device class only. Migration `supabase/migrations/20261029133000_ask_questions.sql` is committed unapplied — Tom's database desk reviews and applies it. Harmless until then. Preview only; Tom merges.
